  ],
  "difficulty": "medium",
  "tags": []
 },
 {
  "id": "1t06-q13",
  "chapterId": "puc1-statistics-06-measures-of-dispersion",
  "topicId": "puc1-statistics-06-measures-of-dispersion.t4",
  "stem": {
   "en": "If the variance of a distribution is 25, its standard deviation is:"
  },
  "options": [
   {
    "en": "625"
   },
   {
    "en": "25"
   },
   {
    "en": "5"
   },
   {
    "en": "12.5"
   }
  ],
  "answer": 2,
  "explanation": {
   "en": "S.D. is the positive square root of the variance: √25 = 5."
  },
  "exams": [
   "PUC"
  ],
  "difficulty": "easy",
  "tags": []
 },
 {
  "id": "1t06-q14",
  "chapterId": "puc1-statistics-06-measures-of-dispersion",
  "topicId": "puc1-statistics-06-measures-of-dispersion.t4",
  "stem": {
   "en": "The standard deviation of 2, 4, 6, 8, 10 is about:"
  },
  "options": [
   {
    "en": "3.16"
   },
   {
    "en": "2.83"
   },
   {
    "en": "2.4"
   },
   {
    "en": "8"
   }
  ],
  "answer": 1,
  "explanation": {
   "en": "Mean = 6; squared deviations 16, 4, 0, 4, 16 sum to 40; variance = 40/5 = 8; S.D. = √8 ≈ 2.83."
  },
  "exams": [
   "PUC"
  ],
  "difficulty": "easy",
  "tags": []
 },
 {
  "id": "1t06-q15",
  "chapterId": "puc1-statistics-06-measures-of-dispersion",
  "topicId": "puc1-statistics-06-measures-of-dispersion.t4",
  "stem": {
   "en": "If 5 is added to every observation, the standard deviation:"
