   "PUC"
  ],
  "difficulty": "easy",
  "tags": []
 },
 {
  "id": "1t06-q16",
  "chapterId": "puc1-statistics-06-measures-of-dispersion",
  "topicId": "puc1-statistics-06-measures-of-dispersion.t4",
  "stem": {
   "en": "For 10 observations, Σx = 50 and Σx² = 290. The standard deviation is:"
  },
  "options": [
   {
    "en": "√29"
   },
   {
    "en": "4"
   },
   {
    "en": "5"
   },
   {
    "en": "2"
   }
  ],
  "answer": 3,
  "explanation": {
   "en": "Mean = 5; σ² = Σx²/n − (mean)² = 29 − 25 = 4; σ = 2."
  },
  "exams": [
   "PUC"
  ],
  "difficulty": "medium",
  "tags": [],
  "solution": [
   {
    "en": "Mean = 5; σ² = Σx²/n − (mean)² = 29 − 25 = 4; σ = 2."
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "id": "1t06-q17",
  "chapterId": "puc1-statistics-06-measures-of-dispersion",
  "topicId": "puc1-statistics-06-measures-of-dispersion.t4",
  "stem": {
   "en": "Every observation is multiplied by 3. If the old S.D. was 4, the new S.D. is:"
  },
  "options": [
   {
    "en": "12"
   },
   {
    "en": "7"
   },
   {
    "en": "4"
   },
   {
    "en": "36"
   }
  ],
  "answer": 0,
  "explanation": {
   "en": "S.D. depends on change of scale: multiplying by k multiplies σ by |k|. New σ = 3 × 4 = 12."
  },
  "exams": [
   "PUC"
  ],
  "difficulty": "medium",
  "tags": []
 },
 {
  "id": "1t06-q18",
  "chapterId": "puc1-statistics-06-measures-of-dispersion",
  "topicId": "puc1-statistics-06-measures-of-dispersion.t5",
  "stem": {
   "en": "If the mean is 40 and the S.D. is 10, the coefficient of variation is:"
  },
  "options": [
   {
    "en": "4%"
   },
   {
    "en": "400%"
   },
   {
    "en": "0.25%"
   },
   {
    "en": "25%"
   }
  ],
  "answer": 3,
  "explanation": {
   "en": "C.V. = σ/x̄ × 100 = 10/40 × 100 = 25%."
  },
  "exams": [
   "PUC"
  ],
  "difficulty": "easy",
  "tags": []
 },
 {
  "id": "1t06-q19",
  "chapterId": "puc1-statistics-06-measures-of-dispersion",
  "topicId": "puc1-statistics-06-measures-of-dispersion.t5",
  "stem": {
   "en": "Of two series, the one with the smaller coefficient of variation is:"
  },
  "options": [
   {
    "en": "larger in mean"
   },
   {
    "en": "more consistent"
   },
   {
    "en": "larger in S.D."
   },
   {
    "en": "more variable"
   }
  ],
  "answer": 1,
  "explanation": {
   "en": "A smaller C.V. means less relative variation, so that series is more consistent (uniform, stable)."
  },
  "exams": [
   "PUC"
  ],
  "difficulty": "easy",
  "tags": []
 },
 {
  "id": "1t06-q20",
  "chapterId": "puc1-statistics-06-measures-of-dispersion",
  "topicId": "puc1-statistics-06-measures-of-dispersion.t5",
  "stem": {
   "en": "Group 1 has 20 items with mean 30; group 2 has 30 items with mean 40. The combined mean is:"
  },
  "options": [
   {
    "en": "34"
   },
   {
    "en": "36"
   },
   {
    "en": "70"
   },
   {
    "en": "35"
   }
  ],
  "answer": 1,
  "explanation": {
   "en": "x̄ = (20 × 30 + 30 × 40)/50 = 1800/50 = 36."
  },
  "exams": [
   "PUC"
  ],
  "difficulty": "easy",
  "tags": []
 },
 {
  "id": "1t06-q21",
  "chapterId": "puc1-statistics-06-measures-of-dispersion",
  "topicId": "puc1-statistics-06-measures-of-dispersion.t5",
  "stem": {
   "en": "If the C.V. is 20% and the S.D. is 6, the mean is:"
