  "tags": []
 },
 {
  "id": "1t06-q22",
  "chapterId": "puc1-statistics-06-measures-of-dispersion",
  "topicId": "puc1-statistics-06-measures-of-dispersion.t5",
  "stem": {
   "en": "Two groups of 50 each have means 10 and 20 and S.D.s 3 and 4. The combined S.D. is about:"
  },
  "options": [
   {
    "en": "3.5"
   },
   {
    "en": "5"
   },
   {
    "en": "6.12"
   },
   {
    "en": "7"
   }
  ],
  "answer": 2,
  "explanation": {
   "en": "Combined mean 15, so d₁ = −5, d₂ = 5. σ² = [50(9 + 25) + 50(16 + 25)]/100 = 37.5; σ = √37.5 ≈ 6.12."
  },
  "exams": [
   "PUC"
  ],
  "difficulty": "hard",
  "tags": [],
  "solution": [
   {
    "en": "Combined mean 15, so d₁ = −5, d₂ = 5. σ² = [50(9 + 25) + 50(16 + 25)]/100 = 37.5; σ = √37.5 ≈ 6.12."
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "id": "1t06-q23",
  "chapterId": "puc1-statistics-06-measures-of-dispersion",
  "topicId": "puc1-statistics-06-measures-of-dispersion.t2",
  "stem": {
   "en": "If the coefficient of quartile deviation is 0.25 and Q₃ = 50, then Q₁ is:"
  },
  "options": [
   {
    "en": "12.5"
   },
   {
    "en": "40"
   },
   {
    "en": "30"
   },
   {
    "en": "37.5"
   }
  ],
  "answer": 2,
  "explanation": {
   "en": "(50 − Q₁)/(50 + Q₁) = 0.25 ⇒ 50 − Q₁ = 12.5 + 0.25Q₁ ⇒ 1.25Q₁ = 37.5 ⇒ Q₁ = 30."
  },
  "exams": [
   "PUC"
  ],
  "difficulty": "medium",
  "tags": []
 },
 {
  "id": "1t06-q24",
  "chapterId": "puc1-statistics-06-measures-of-dispersion",
  "topicId": "puc1-statistics-06-measures-of-dispersion.t4",
  "stem": {
   "en": "The sum of squares of deviations of a set of values is least when taken about the:"
  },
  "options": [
   {
    "en": "median"
   },
   {
    "en": "mode"
   },
   {
    "en": "origin"
   },
   {
    "en": "arithmetic mean"
   }
  ],
  "answer": 3,
  "explanation": {
   "en": "Σ(x − A)² is minimum when A = x̄; this is why S.D. is measured about the mean."
  },
  "exams": [
   "PUC"
  ],
  "difficulty": "easy",
  "tags": []
 },
 {
